WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:24.180
Hi John! Good morning! It's Brotherhood 2.0
with Hank and John Green!

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:31.640
Wow, that guy was having fun. It's seven o'clock
in the morning and I'm about to get on a plane.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:37.120
Yesterday I was sledding down a hill at Lake
Tahoe. That was fun; this isn't fun.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.510
I hope you don't mind if I make a suggestion
as to how to begin our conversation on this

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:46.430
video blog. Being your brother is kinda frustrating
sometimes. This is because people walk up

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:52.470
to me and they say, "Gosh, you look so much
like your brother. Oh, your jokes are very

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:58.010
similar to your brother's, except you're not
quite as funny as him." Apparently some people

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.330
even think that we look like the twin rock
duo, The Proclaimers, which is admittedly

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:07.750
better than people thinking that we look like
the twin rock duo, Nelson.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:14.440
So, I would like to propose a list. We make
a video blog list of all the ways in which

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.430
we are very, very different people.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:23.030
Things like: in the last few years John Green
has gotten kind of pudgy. Whereas, in the

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:29.760
next few years Hank Green will get kind of
pudgy. And also things like: John Green has

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.580
never spilled a tiny amount of beer on his
wife's MacBook, which then proceeded to not

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:41.060
boot up. And also, John Green didn't almost
ruin the video blog experiment by not having

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:46.330
a computer that would work. And also, John
Green didn't do the Happy Dance when his wife

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:51.030
was in the shower, and he reinstalled the
battery and tried to boot it up the next morning

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:59.480
and it worked. (dances) And also, John Green
probably would have told his wife about the

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:07.479
incident instead of hoping everything would
turn out okay. Sorry honey!

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:17.580
And also, and also, and also. And also John
Green doesn't constantly and vainly obsess

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.540
about his hair, which apparently I do. On
some level, performing a version of 500 Miles

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:30.030
on this show actually does appeal to me. Punishment,
project, or challenge?

